{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 35, "timestamp": 1778688128, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-color"}, "title": "craftcargo: Rust Crate \u2192 .deb in Seconds"}
[0.0164955, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J"]
[0.0174855, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[0;36m\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[0;37m        craftcargo: Rust \u2192 Ubuntu Packaging Made Easy\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[0;36m\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0;90mThis demo shows how craftcargo generates a complete debcraft.yaml\r\nfrom a Rust crate, ready for Ubuntu package building.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[3.0262545000000003, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Step 1: Let's see what craftcargo can do\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.035537999999999, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mdebcargo --help\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.046635, "o", "Package Rust crates for Debian.\r\n\r\n\u001b[32mUsage:\u001b[0m \u001b[32mdebcargo\u001b[0m \u001b[32m<COMMAND>\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[33mCommands:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[32mupdate\u001b[0m               Update the user's default crates.io index, outside of a workspace\r\n  \u001b[32mdeb-src-name\u001b[0m         Print the Debian package name for a crate\r\n  \u001b[32mextract\u001b[0m              Extract only a crate, without any other transformations\r\n  \u001b[32mpackage\u001b[0m              Package a Rust crate for Debian\r\n  \u001b[32mpackage-debcraft\u001b[0m     Package a Rust crate for debcraft (generates debcraft.yaml)\r\n  \u001b[32mbuild-order\u001b[0m          Print the transitive dependencies of a package in topological order\r\n  \u001b[32mdeb-dependencies\u001b[0m     Print the dependencies of a package in d/control format\r\n  \u001b[32mupdate-dependencies\u001b[0m  Update debian/control Build-Depends from workspace Cargo.toml files\r\n  \u001b[32mhelp\u001b[0m                 Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\r\n\r\n\u001b[33mOptions:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[32m-h\u001b[0m, \u001b[32m--help\u001b[0m     Print help\r\n  \u001b[32m-V\u001b[0m, \u001b[32m--version\u001b[0m  Print version\r\n"]
[6.0561359999999995, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Step 2: Let's package 'bon' \u2014 a popular builder-pattern macro crate\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.056175, "o", "\r\n"]
[6.059918999999999, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# First, what would the Debian source package be called?\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.570305, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mdebcargo deb-src-name bon\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.638583499999999, "o", "bon\r\n"]
[7.6506615, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Step 3: Generate the debcraft.yaml\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.1615875, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mdebcargo package-debcraft bon --directory ./output/bon\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.1865085, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[92m    Updating\u001b[0m crates.io index\r\n"]
[9.9487185, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[96m       Fetch\u001b[0m [=====>                           ] 0 complete; 1 pending                            \r"]
[11.470286999999999, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[96m       Fetch\u001b[0m [========>                        ] 2 complete; 0 pending                            \r"]
[11.480601, "o", "\u001b[K"]
[11.563975500000002, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Step 4: Let's look at what was generated\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[13.072369499999999, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mls ./output/bon/\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[13.0787685, "o", "Cargo.lock  Cargo.toml.orig  LICENSE-MIT  debcraft\t src\r\nCargo.toml  LICENSE-APACHE   README.md\t  debcraft.yaml\t tests\r\n"]
[14.591113499999999, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Here's the debcraft.yaml:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.100106, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mcat ./output/bon/debcraft.yaml\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.107312, "o", "name: rust-bon\r\nversion: 3.9.1-1\r\nsummary: Next-gen compile-time-checked builder generator, named function's \u2026\r\ndescription: Description\r\nmaintainer: Debian Rust Maintainers <pkg-rust-maintainers@alioth-lists.debian.net>\r\nsection: rust\r\ncontact: Debian Rust Maintainers <pkg-rust-maintainers@alioth-lists.debian.net>\r\nsource-code: https://bon-rs.com\r\nlicense: MIT OR Apache-2.0\r\nissues: https://github.com/elastio/bon/issues\r\nparts:\r\n  crate:\r\n    plugin: dump\r\n    source: .\r\npackages:\r\n  librust-bon-alloc-dev:\r\n    architectures: any\r\n    summary: Next-gen compile-time-checked builder generator, named function's \u2026\r\n    description: This metapackage enables feature \"alloc\" for the Rust bon crate, by pulling in any additional dependencies needed by that feature.\r\n    depends:\r\n    - librust-bon-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-alloc-dev (<< 3.9.2)\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-alloc-dev (>= 3.9.1)\r\n    provides:\r\n    - librust-bon-3-alloc-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9-alloc-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9.1-alloc-dev\r\n    breaks:\r\n    - rustc (<< 1.59.0~)\r\n    multi-arch: same\r\n  librust-bon-dev:\r\n    architectures: any\r\n    summary: Next-gen compile-time-checked builder generator, named function's \u2026\r\n    description: Source code for Debianized Rust crate \"bon\"\r\n    depends:\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-default-dev (<< 3.9.2)\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-default-dev (>= 3.9.1)\r\n    - librust-rustversion-1-default-dev\r\n    recommends:\r\n    - librust-bon-std-dev\r\n    suggests:\r\n    - librust-bon-alloc-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-experimental-generics-setters-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-experimental-overwritable-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-implied-bounds-dev\r\n    provides:\r\n    - librust-bon-experimental-getter-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3-experimental-getter-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9-experimental-getter-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9.1-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9.1-experimental-getter-dev\r\n    breaks:\r\n    - rustc (<< 1.59.0~)\r\n    multi-arch: same\r\n  librust-bon-experimental-generics-setters-dev:\r\n    architectures: any\r\n    summary: Next-gen compile-time-checked builder generator, named function's \u2026\r\n    description: This metapackage enables feature \"experimental-generics-setters\" for the Rust bon crate, by pulling in any additional dependencies needed by that feature.\r\n    depends:\r\n    - librust-bon-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-experimental-generics-setters-dev (<< 3.9.2)\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-experimental-generics-setters-dev (>= 3.9.1)\r\n    provides:\r\n    - librust-bon-3-experimental-generics-setters-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9-experimental-generics-setters-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9.1-experimental-generics-setters-dev\r\n    breaks:\r\n    - rustc (<< 1.59.0~)\r\n    multi-arch: same\r\n  librust-bon-experimental-overwritable-dev:\r\n    architectures: any\r\n    summary: Next-gen compile-time-checked builder generator, named function's \u2026\r\n    description: This metapackage enables feature \"experimental-overwritable\" for the Rust bon crate, by pulling in any additional dependencies needed by that feature.\r\n    depends:\r\n    - librust-bon-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-experimental-overwritable-dev (<< 3.9.2)\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-experimental-overwritable-dev (>= 3.9.1)\r\n    provides:\r\n    - librust-bon-3-experimental-overwritable-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9-experimental-overwritable-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9.1-experimental-overwritable-dev\r\n    breaks:\r\n    - rustc (<< 1.59.0~)\r\n    multi-arch: same\r\n  librust-bon-implied-bounds-dev:\r\n    architectures: any\r\n    summary: Next-gen compile-time-checked builder generator, named function's \u2026\r\n    description: This metapackage enables feature \"implied-bounds\" for the Rust bon crate, by pulling in any additional dependencies needed by that feature.\r\n    depends:\r\n    - librust-bon-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-implied-bounds-dev (<< 3.9.2)\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-implied-bounds-dev (>= 3.9.1)\r\n    provides:\r\n    - librust-bon-3-implied-bounds-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9-implied-bounds-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9.1-implied"]
[16.10751, "o", "-bounds-dev\r\n    breaks:\r\n    - rustc (<< 1.59.0~)\r\n    multi-arch: same\r\n  librust-bon-std-dev:\r\n    architectures: any\r\n    summary: Next-gen compile-time-checked builder generator, named function's \u2026\r\n    description: |-\r\n      This metapackage enables feature \"std\" for the Rust bon crate, by pulling in any additional dependencies needed by that feature.\r\n\r\n      Additionally, this package also provides the \"default\" feature.\r\n    depends:\r\n    - librust-bon-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-alloc-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-std-dev (<< 3.9.2)\r\n    - librust-bon-macros-3.9-std-dev (>= 3.9.1)\r\n    provides:\r\n    - librust-bon-default-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3-std-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3-default-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9-std-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9-default-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9.1-std-dev\r\n    - librust-bon-3.9.1-default-dev\r\n    breaks:\r\n    - rustc (<< 1.59.0~)\r\n    multi-arch: same\r\n"]
[16.116076500000002, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Step 5: Now let's build the .deb packages \u2014 one command!\u001b[0m\r\n"]
